WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Shlomo HaMelech was already appointed as king before David died, and so far he's not doing anything because his father is alive.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Now, when father dies, there's going to be a movie, where Shlomo HaMelech is the main character,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:41.000
and the name of the movie is, Home Alone. All right? And, and heads, I don't know, roll. All right? Very good.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.640
And the guy is very smart.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.220
And what do you know at this time?

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.460
At the time he's 12 years old.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:47.840
Alright?

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.320
There is nothing more ferocious

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.800
than a 12 years old boy.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:54.960
Alright? Nothing more ferocious than that.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:56.760
Right? Now.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:02.840
And the days of David

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:04.760
were near to die.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.700
In other words, he felt that he was about to die.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.020
And many people say,

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:10.440
also Haramban and so on,

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:17.360
that when a person is about to die, you know, they know, they have a premonition, you know,

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:19.480
they know that they're going to die.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:25.060
And now, something which became almost part of the Jewish custom,

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.600
it's part of the, that's a real minhag.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:31.600
V'esat et shelobo v'enolam levot.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:33.580
And he, v'osah.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:39.960
V'osah is the last will that the person has for his family.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:52.380
and the wassion, same thing like baisat, it's used in Arabic, or every wassani means that is the last will of the parents,

00:01:52.800 --> 00:02:00.180
and the parents, they have an obligation to make a less will for his children.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:05.080
Now, the last will here is not like the American last will.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.800
The American last will is, where am I going to have it with my money?

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:16.800
In Jewish law, there is this law of inheritance. So the money is automatically, there is nothing you can do about it.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.800
The money, if it's Mechorik, it's twice, or whatever it is.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:27.800
The word Saba'ah, last will, which comes from the Bible by some, this is the last will, before he dies,

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:32.800
it means what you want him to do for you. You see?

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:38.800
And now we're going to see what David wants him to do, and how Shalom Ha-Mendit is going to take it.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:41.800
Alright? Now, he says,

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:45.800
,

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:49.800
My father says,

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:53.800
We're all on the same path, you know, we're all on the same road,

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:58.800
and I am going in the road that the whole world has to go through,

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.800
which is death. Now,

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:06.800
behazakta ya'ita la'ish. The first

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:10.800
part of the, of the, of this

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.800
legacy that he leaves for her is behazakta

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:18.800
Oh, shalom aleichem.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.800
Shalom aleichem. Baruch haba, sit down please.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:26.800
Alright, so now the first thing that

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:29.720
that he says,

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:34.420
you should become strong,

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:36.200
characterized,

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:41.220
because a person who has an enormous amount of intelligence,

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:44.300
like King Shalom,

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.200
he has one problem.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:49.720
How do you manage that intelligence?

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:54.780
You will see the great failure of King Shalom,

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:58.780
is that he was unable to manage that intelligence.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.780
And the Serbian says,

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:03.780
, strong personality.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:08.780
, and you should become a man.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:14.780
Now you're a child, you should become a man.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:19.780
And you're going to see that he takes this in the wrong way, I believe.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:22.780
You're going to see exactly what he's going to do.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.380
And, but the first he says,

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:27.380
Ve-chazakta ve-ayitare ish.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.380
Nobody's going to have a new role now.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.380
Forget that you're, you're...

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:34.380
The fact that you're 12 years old,

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:36.380
yes, he was to have chosen all the time,

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:39.380
well, now you have to, ve-chazakta,

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.380
Yes, be a man.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.380
Be a man, right.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:44.380
You see, you see,

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.380
in my opinion, that's my opinion, you know,

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:48.380
I, you know, everybody loves Shimon Melech,

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:50.380
I'm not a great fan of Shimon Melech,

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:52.380
although the whole Jewish people love him.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:58.380
I think you're going to see why, all right? I'm not a great fan of him. I know that he was intelligent and so on,

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:05.380
but I don't know whether politically he was, you know, whether he was politically intelligent or not, all right?

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:12.380
Now, he's going to tell them, first, it's a question of human. You cannot be Jewish if you're not human.

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:17.380
You could be Jewish if you're not a human being. You cannot be Jewish.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:18.380
So the first thing is,

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.380
V'chazakta v'ayita le'ish.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.380
Second,

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:25.380
Mishamarta it mishmeret Adonai Elohecha.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:31.380
You must observe the laws that God gave you.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:35.380
In other words, mishmeret always means the provisions.

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:39.380
Be careful, do not transgress any of the provisions.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:40.380
Yes?

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:43.380
And also, the B'Sad Haseh,

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:48.180
and to follow the ways of God.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.140
Quickly,

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:53.700
,

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.820
you have to observe all the laws.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:06:01.540
There's Chokim, Chokim are the laws that we ritual, we don't know the meaning of it.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:06.540
Mishpat, yes, , things like this.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:13.180
Mishpatav, judicial process, yes, procedure, legal procedure.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:18.580
and the testimony, means the holidays that testified for great events in the past,

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:21.900
like Pesach, like Sukkot, like Shavuot,

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:26.480
that each one is a testimony to a great national event.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:30.760
And you do it not the way you think it should be done,

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.280
but it's written in the Book of Moshem.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:38.520
And you have to do it according to what is written in the Law of Moses.

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:45.520
so that you'll be successful in whatever you do.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:54.520
And wherever you want to turn your face there, then you're going to succeed.

00:06:54.520 --> 00:07:01.520
This Passover is a very important Passover because it almost tells you the whole philosophy of King David.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:04.520
A few things, I want to point out a few things.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:12.520
Number one, King David was the greatest king, in my opinion, in the opinion of most Jews

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:20.520
that King David was the greatest king we had. And I believe because of two very, very important things.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:28.520
Number one, he was the king that fought for and achieved political integrity.

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:44.400
In other words, we were a political entity. Before King David, we were 12 tribes. And he worked throughout his life in order that these 12 tribes should integrate and become a single nation.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:08:09.240
The task of a king is not to be nice or not to be nice, to be fair or to be unfair. The first task of the king is the political health of the nation, to make sure that politically his decisions will bear positive fruit.

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:20.240
Even justice, yes, is not as important as what is politically healthy or not.

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:25.240
Let me give you an example of a contemporary issue. Take the case of Hebron.

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:28.240
I don't think the judge made right, wrong, right. Let's just take it.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:33.240
From my point of view, as I understand it, the most important thing of the political leader is

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:40.240
Was it fair? Was it unfair? Is it right? Is it wrong?

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:51.240
But the question is, what would be the political consequences if I choose A or B or C?

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:55.240
Would this make Israel stronger? Yes? All right?

00:08:55.240 --> 00:09:04.240
Will this bring a further development in the growth, in the political growth?

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:12.240
Those are the most important things. So, King David was the one who understood

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:19.240
the political dimension of the Jewish people, and he worked tirelessly to obtain this.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:28.240
But, that would be nothing, it would be because of what he's saying now to King Solomon.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:37.240
Namely that we are a constitutional monarchy. Throughout history, the monarch does exactly what he or she pleases.

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:41.240
The monarch is the source of right and wrong.

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:49.540
In Judaism, the monarch is under the law, and therefore here it says,

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:50.900
you have to

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:54.920
v'shamartat v'shmeret Adonai Elohecha, l'alekhet l'drachav, v'shmerchot potav,

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:57.080
z'vat, kat katub l'trad Mosheh.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:06.540
So here it is the obligation of the king to follow the law.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:21.040
We do not have, for instance, among, say, Persia, Assyria, Babylonia, all these kingdoms, or the Greeks, or so on, the whole notion of a constitutional monarch.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:26.540
This does not exist. So here we have it. All right? That's one thing.

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:34.540
Second, I like very, very much the word Tazkir. The word Tazkir comes from the word Seher. All right?

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:42.960
intelligence. And here the word taskil means not intelligence, but means success.

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:48.180
So now here David Al-Melef is using the word taskil for success.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:56.140
Leman taskil et kol hajeta'aseh. So here in the Vedic thing you have the philosophy of success.

00:10:56.140 --> 00:11:02.440
If you understand what you're doing, then you are successful in what you're doing.

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:06.940
Success and understanding come hand in hand.

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:09.940
There is no such thing as being successful

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:12.940
if you do not understand what you are doing.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:16.940
It is not luck.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:19.940
You cannot search for luck.

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:22.440
What you could search for is

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:25.440
لَمَا تَسْكِلْ

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:26.440
to understand,

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:28.440
and قَلْ أَشَرْ تَعْسَدْ

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:30.440
That is very important.

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:36.940
Right? Fine. Now, if you're going to do these three things,

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:41.320
Ha'ita le'ish, personality means ethics and so on,

00:11:42.140 --> 00:11:45.400
Shamatal, observe the Torah, yes?

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:49.840
And Shamatal b'shmet Adonai Eloheka,

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:54.940
and you do everything, the third thing, you recognize the Torah as the supreme law of Israel,

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:56.940
then,

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:00.940
,

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:02.940
God made me a promise,

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:04.940
saying, your children,

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.940
yes, say like this,

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:10.940
,

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:12.940
if your children follow my

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:14.940
path, not their path,

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:16.940
it's submission to the higher authority.

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:20.940
,

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:22.940
Just like in the K'yat Shema,

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:24.940
Lecholev Ha'vichra, Ucholam Shechecha.

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:26.940
Then God made the promise,

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:30.940
Lo yikaret lecha ish me'akeseh

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:37.940
Never one of your heirs will be cut off from Israel.

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:39.940
So the promise is a very important promise.

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:42.940
God made a promise to King David.

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:47.940
Your children will always be sitting on the throne,

00:12:47.940 --> 00:12:49.580
not of Yehudah,

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:51.480
but of Israel,

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:52.760
you know, the whole nation.

00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:56.020
But when God makes a promise,

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:57.920
never God

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.140
makes a promise in a vacuum.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:01.540
It's always within a context.

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:03.820
And the context is

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:06.100
a kingdom

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:07.380
that follows

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:09.980
the Torah. So therefore,

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:11.440
yes, God made me a promise,

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:13.240
but the promise is conditional.

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:15.420
Conditional to your

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:17.500
following

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:19.860
the path of the Torah.

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:22.060
Otherwise, the

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:23.160
promise would not be fulfilled.

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:25.600
And in point of fact, you will see

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:27.800
that I, again, I'm

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:29.680
not a pro-Salomon

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:31.220
man.

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:32.980
And I, Solomon,

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:35.360
he was a, he

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:37.540
sown the seed of

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:39.440
descent already during his

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:41.560
kingdom, and immediately after he died,

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:42.680
then there's the

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:45.460
Israel split into two,

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:47.480
and the whole, what

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:55.480
King David said he was fulfilled. He himself, King David, did not fulfill the Torah, in two basic things, we're going to see later on.

00:13:55.480 --> 00:14:05.480
King Solomon, I'm sorry, did not fulfill the Torah, and therefore his throne was split immediately after his death.

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:16.480
And we lost ten tribes, and we, the other two tribes, which is Benjamin and Yehudah, we are the children of Benjamin and Yehudah,

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:18.120
we are in Galut.

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:22.980
No, we lost

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:25.040
in Galut, but the Galut would never

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:27.100
have come if they would

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:28.180
not split.

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:30.780
Once we split into two,

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:32.980
we were vulnerable. If we would

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:34.680
have been one united nation,

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:36.360
a nation united,

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:38.960
no kingdom in the world would be able to

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:41.120
and so we were

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:43.400
defeated because King Solomon

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:45.220
was

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:51.140
unable to carry on the promise of King David. And that's why, I mean, the Mashiach is David,

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:57.740
is the symbol of the Mashiach Israel. The first king is the first symbol of the last king,

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:00.280
you know, which is going to be the Mashiach, you know. Interesting.

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:01.660
Yeah, that's true.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:02.160
Yes.

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:04.980
And when he carried the third Israel, he said Israel.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:09.940
Israel, I didn't say Yehudah. Israel means the entire nation.

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:14.940
Obviously, King David did not see. He did not fulfill the end.

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:17.940
The king would not die while he's...

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:21.940
Yeah, it means nobody is going to dethrone him.

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:24.940
There's not going to be no insurrection at the end.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:28.940
Nobody would be successful in chopping him out.

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:30.940
And his family.

00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:34.940
Yeah, but in other words, he would have a stable thing now.

00:15:34.940 --> 00:15:45.940
Now, on the other hand, it's interesting. With all the turmoil, the dynasty of David lasted for 400 and some years.

00:15:45.940 --> 00:15:51.940
It was one of the longest dynasties in the history of royalty.

00:15:51.940 --> 00:15:57.940
Yes, it's an extraordinary thing. With all the problems and so on, it lasted for, you know, and still,

00:15:57.940 --> 00:16:00.160
What does it mean, people don't understand, what does it mean the Mashiach?

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:04.980
Mashiach means the restoration of David's dynasty.

00:16:05.780 --> 00:16:07.140
Because the Mashiach had to live in David.

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:09.240
Alright.

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:10.780
And that means the restoration.

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:17.040
It means that after 3500 years, still we say, we want the dynasty of David.

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:22.520
So, there is no other nation.

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:23.100
Alright.

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:37.100
Um, the Gamata now, that he promised, he gave him, made him a wasi, a saba'o, a saba'a, the last word,

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:47.100
first he tell him about the important things, now personal things, and now he's going to ask his son to commit political vengeance.

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:54.100
vengeance.

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:58.340
Yoav ben Zerah was a general, very, very successful,

00:16:58.340 --> 00:17:01.700
apparently a great general, but also

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:06.040
a very treacherous and very bloodthirsty individual, and he did

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:09.380
two things that King David

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:13.220
felt bad about it, that King David was

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:16.580
in a position, a vulnerable position.

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:21.000
So he could not get rid of Yoav and Seryal,

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:27.160
and therefore he asked Solomon to avenge.

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:31.480
And now we're going to speak about vengeance and so on in a few minutes, all right?

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:33.680
But let's first see what happened.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:39.000
It says, now privacy.

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:41.620
He said, that's why they got.

